"""wh: willhaben.at from the terminal. Fast public data with a local cache; Claude does the judging.

Data commands (no AI):  search, ad, photos, status, sweep
AI commands:            deal, advise, hunt   (gather the data, then ask `claude -p` with the willhaben skill's rules;
                                              --no-ai prints the gathered data instead, for use inside a Claude session)

Every ad wh sees goes into ~/.local/share/wh/wh.db (price history, "new since last sweep"). Notes are read from
~/Notes/Marketplace. Only public pages are read; anything behind the login stays with Claude in Chrome.
"""
